        UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT\n\n                                   5                                  NORTHERN DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA\n\n                                   6\n\n                                   7     MICHAEL MURPHY, et al.,                            Case No. 25-cv-04036-EKL (SVK)\n                                   8                    Plaintiffs,\n                                                                                            ORDER RE CONFLICT DISCLOSURE\n                                   9             v.\n\n                                  10     LINKEDIN CORPORATION,\n                                  11                    Defendant.\n\n                                  12          It has recently come to the Court\u2019s attention that from the period January 1, 2026 to\nNorthern District of California\n United States District Court\n\n\n\n\n                                  13   April 13, 2026 the undersigned had a conflict of interest in this matter. That conflict has now been\n                                  14   resolved and no longer exists. During this time period, the undersigned did not work on this\n                                  15   matter and issued no orders. Within seven days of the date of this Order, any Party may file a\n                                  16   Notice of Objection referring to this Order. No other basis for objection is required. If a Notice of\n                                  17   Objection is filed, the undersigned will recuse from this matter. The case will be reassigned to a\n                                  18   discovery referral judge.\n                                  19          SO ORDERED.\n                                  20   Dated: April 16, 2026\n                                  21\n\n                                  22\n                                                                                                    SUSAN VAN KEULEN\n                            